        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "మల్లెపువ్వు (mallepuvvu) is malle, \"jasmine\", which matches Sanskrit mallikā, \"jasmine\" (CDIAL 9913), and native puvvu, \"flower\" (DEDR 4345). CDIAL compares the Dravidian jasmine words with the Sanskrit one; DEDR compares, with a query, Sanskrit puṣpa, \"flower\", with puvvu."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
